==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Catclaw Castle (Enemy Base)|Catclaw Castle]].
*3 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*2 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 8.67 seconds<sup>260f</sup>, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 60~73.33 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Midnite D.]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Sir Rel]] spawns after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Masked Okame]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Sir Seal]]s spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
**2 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**1 [[Vermilingua Rangmaster]] spawns.
**1 [[Ancient Magamojoe]] spawns after 63.33 seconds<sup>1,900f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 53.33~56.67 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Generally considered to be the scariest stage in the entirety of Catclaw Championships, Rank 12's Rank-Up Test 3 is a true test of endurance for even skilled players. However, even a stage with a schematic like this can fall to stacked [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeyes]] and [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cats]].

Start by defeating the five Sir Seals, Sir Rel, then stalling the Midnite D. with [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]] until you have a small stack of Sniper the Deadeyes and Cyberpunk Cats (two of each). Then, once they're at around half cooldown, spawn [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] and [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]], and let them handle the Midnite D. By the time they reach the base, Uril should be off cooldown.

Your main objective is to either defeat Vermilingua Rangmaster or severely cripple him before Ancient Magamojoe spawns and tears through your defenses. This is made difficult by the Masked Okame that spawns alongside Rangmaster as the boss; Okame's low range, high damage and incredible pushing power with guaranteed [[Knockback]] make it almost impossible to single out the Rangmaster through conventional means. This leaves only a few realistic non-[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]]/[[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare]] options, those being Esoteric Uril and Ape Lord Luza. Both of them have [[Behemoth Slayer]], and Uril has [[Strong Against|Strong VS]] Relic and Aku. They can gradually wear him down over time as long as you keep Okame at a distance using Cyberpunk Cat and Sniper the Deadeye. At this point, you will want to refrain from sending out any meatshields, as they will do more harm than good due to triggering Okame's [[Omni Strike]]. Rangmaster will occasionally absorb Sniper the Deadeye's attacks, which is normal, but do keep [[Cat Cannon|Breakerblast]] on hold until Okame gets dangerously close to your Sniperpunk stack.

To further add insult to injury, Sir Seals, Sir Rels, and Sinner Snaches will continuously spawn purely to make your life more difficult. Ordinarily, you would expect the Sir Rels to be the problem peons of this stage. And with their incredibly high speed, HP, and DPS, they certainly are an issue. However, the bigger threat by far is the Sir Seals that spawn every 20 seconds: with each having '''150,000''' HP and 12,000 DPS, they are both your only source of income and your biggest nightmare. Their incredible bulk means they can shrug off most attacks, including [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cats]], [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycats]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cats]], and even [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]] at higher extremes. You will need to bring a few dedicated counters for these guys, since when left unchecked they will shred your ranged attackers like Esoteric Uril.

Due to the preceding factors, your Urils will typically fall right before defeating Rangmaster, leaving him with 1/4 HP. At this point, Magamojoe will spawn, and your Ape Lord Luza will go off cooldown. Lure Magamojoe and Rangmaster to your base, and spawn Ape Lord Luza to deal with the rest of his HP. When the time is right, spawn Idi:NX to swiftly take care of Magamojoe. (Another possible scenario is that you actually defeat Rangmaster before Magamojoe spawns. In this situation, luring him to your base is still the way to go, but the process of taking him out will be far quicker and easier.)

If you pulled all of these steps off correctly, congratulations! You're almost done, but now you have to survive Okame. At this point, there are a few selectable options for keeping her at bay: [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] can hold the front lines for some time up until the Sir Rels and Sinner Snaches spawn to ruin everything. [[Talents|Talented]] [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydance Cat]] can [[Dodge]] [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] and [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies. Talented [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]] or Courier Cat can rush in to deal high damage to Okame, the former [[Weaken]]ing her. This final step will take a long time to pull off, and there is still a reasonable chance of failure, so stay on high alert. Cyberpunk and Sniper the Deadeye should greatly aid in keeping Okame at bay though.

Once Okame is defeated, you have beaten the stage.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]] - Wouldn't you know it, Phonoa can help immensely when beating down Vermilingua Rangmaster. Their high health, high range, and ridiculous DPS against traited enemies prove to be an immensely useful asset for chipping at Masked Okame, severely weakening the Sir Seals/Rels, and quickening Rangmaster's demise. Keeping them safe shouldn't be too big of a concern either, with their tendency to stay put, far off from any potential dangers. Phonoa almost trivializes the stage—almost.
*[[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Extinction Phono]] - Just like their [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] counterpart, they serve a near-identical role in this strategy. However, they can be seen as more of a comfort pick, exchanging raw, indiscriminate damage and some range for Area Slow against all enemies on the field. In a strategy that relies entirely on slow, it should be clear why King of Extinction Phonoa is an excellent pick for this stage.
*[[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Dawnbringer Izanagi]] - Just like Phonoa, Izanagi specializes in raw damage. Unlike Phonoa, Izanagi also has the [[Conjure]] ability, which allows him to push back and slow all enemies on the field once. This comes at the cost of low range, lack of Area Attack, and some inconsistent targeting. Despite this, his Single Attack damage when boosted more than makes up for his losses.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]] - Yukimura has [[Massive Damage]] against [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark Enemies]] and [[Strengthen]]. At level 60+, with max Talents, Yukimura can almost take down Masked Okame entirely on his own. This opens the door to potential rush strategies but can also help immensely when Okame is the last enemy standing.
*[[Uesugi Kenshin (Uber Rare Cat)|Hellrider Kenshin]] - Hellrider Kenshin's knockback, quick attack rate and Mini-Wave allow them to shut down Okame from afar, keeping Okame knocked back and unable to attack while other Cats deal with the Rangmaster and Magamojoe. Her Curse Immunity Talent is important because of Magamojoe's Surges, and her Target Relic Talent helps boost her stats against Magamojoe and Sir Rel.
*Ultra Talented [[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine MK3]] - Cat Machine actually finds a unique usefulness during the final stages of the fight. By unlocking its [[Immune to Knockback]] Talent, Masked Okame's main gimmick becomes worthless, and Ultra Talented Cat Machine can begin to stall Okame and the Sir Seals almost indefinitely with over 1,000,000 effective HP against Reds and absolutely no drawbacks. [[Immune to Curse]] also guarantees it doesn't lose its resistances, leaving Sinner Snache to be its only true counter.
*[[Kaoru Hanayama (Uber Rare Cat)|Kaoru Hanayama CC]] - His insane stats against Vermilingua Rangmaster and loads of resistances allow him to decimate it if properly defended, being able to 2-shot it at level 36. Note that this will require luring on base hit so Hanayama doesn't get obliterated by Okame and Sir Rels.
*[[Squire Luno (Uber Rare Cat)|Squire Luno]] - Being one of the best [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]], Squire Luno performs exceptionally well here. With his extremely high defense against target traits he is able to survive a lot of hits by the main threats of this stage, along with his knockback and conjure, which prove to be extremely beneficial at gaining ground. To add to this, he also has a knockback immunity, which makes Okame's gimmick useless against him.
*[[Inosuke Hashibira (Uber Rare Cat)|Inosuke Hashibara]] - Inosuke works extremely well in this stage, as he can crowd-control for a long time before Ancient Magamojoe appears. He also synergizes well with other backliners as he can stop Masked Okame from pushing too hard and killing them.

